  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a differentially private variational quantum classifier trained with gradient clipping and Gaussian noise. On simulated circuits, the model classifies MNIST digits 0 vs 1 with up to 96.5% accuracy using 288 parameters (vs 92.9% for a classical NN with 1029 parameters at ε≈0.406) and achieves up to ~100% accuracy on small 2D benchmark datasets. All experiments are performed on noiseless simulators using at most 10 qubits.",
